<!--
  OWASP Dependency-Check suppression file.

  Rules (see docs/DEPENDENCY_SECURITY.md):
    1. A suppression is allowed only for a confirmed false positive or a
       vulnerability that is not reachable in CareerOS, with a written
       justification.
    2. Every suppression MUST carry an `until` date. Expired suppressions are
       removed/re-reviewed; dependency-check reports them as expired.
    3. Never suppress to make CI green without review, and never suppress a
       HIGH/CRITICAL finding that is reachable.
    4. Do not use `<cvssBelow>` blanket suppressions.

  The file is intentionally empty until a real reviewed exception exists.
-->
